        <mxCell id="UAapYPx3aQhLVE111kwA-637" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 50px;&quot;&gt;An&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;FQDN tag&lt;/b&gt; represents a group of fully qualified domain names (FQDNs) associated&lt;br&gt;with well known Microsoft services.You can use an FQDN tag in &lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 102);&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;application rules&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt; to allow the&lt;br&gt;required &lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 153);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;&quot;&gt;outbound&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;network traffic&lt;/span&gt; through your firewall.&lt;/font&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" parent="I4nSlObdzHv6P_rm0cAF-11" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="-9828" y="4875" width="2119" height="195" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="UAapYPx3aQhLVE111kwA-638" value="&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 0in 0in 0in 0.375in; color: rgb(22, 22, 22);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Comic Sans MS&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 57px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 153);&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;A service tag&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Comic Sans MS&quot; style=&quot;background-color: white; font-size: 40px;&quot;&gt; represents a group of IP address prefixes to help minimize complexity for security rule creation. You can’t create your own service tag, nor specify which IP addresses are included within a tag. Microsoft manages the address prefixes encompassed by the service tag, and automatically updates the service tag as addresses change.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Comic Sans MS&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 40px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 0in 0in 0in 0.375in; color: rgb(22, 22, 22); font-size: 40px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Comic Sans MS&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 40px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: white;&quot;&gt;Azure&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;Firewall &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;service tags can be used in the n&lt;/span&gt;etwork rules destination field.&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt; You can use them in place of&lt;br&gt;specific IP addresses.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Comic Sans MS&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 40px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 40px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;ul type=&quot;disc&quot; style=&quot;direction: ltr; unicode-bidi: embed; margin-top: 0in; font-size: 40px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;vertical-align:middle;color:#161616&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Comic Sans MS&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 40px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: white;&quot;&gt;Is usable in&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/firewall/service-tags&quot;&gt;Azure Firewall&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(22, 22, 22); background: white;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;rulesas a&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-style: italic; color: rgb(22, 22, 22); background: white;&quot;&gt;d&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-style: italic; color: rgb(22, 22, 22); background: yellow;&quot;&gt;estination&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background: yellow;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;rule only for inbound or outbound traffic&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;ul type=&quot;disc&quot; style=&quot;direction: ltr; unicode-bidi: embed; margin-top: 0in; font-size: 40px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; vertical-align: middle;&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Comic Sans MS&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 40px;&quot;&gt;You can use service tags to define network access controls on&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-network/network-security-groups-overview#security-rules&quot;&gt;network&amp;nbsp;security&amp;nbsp;groups&lt;/a&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/firewall/service-tags&quot;&gt;Azure&amp;nbsp;Firewall&lt;/a&gt;, and user-defined routes&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" parent="I4nSlObdzHv6P_rm0cAF-11" vertex="1">
